        "original_id": "f7be5762-1891-5936-8622-3f3c8ab5b9c5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mikhail Lomonosov\n- Products: Akademik Lomonosov\n- Organizations: Bilibino Nuclear Power Plant\n- Concepts: Law of Mass Conservation, atmosphere of Venus\n- Topics: Russian science, literature, education\n\nFacts:\n- Mikhail Vasilyevich Lomonosov lived from 1711 to 1765 and was a Russian polymath, scientist, and writer.\n- Mikhail Lomonosov made important contributions to literature, education, and science.\n- Mikhail Lomonosov's discoveries included the atmosphere of Venus and the Law of Mass Conservation in chemical reactions.\n- Mikhail Lomonosov worked in natural science, chemistry, physics, mineralogy, history, art, philology, and optical devices.\n- The ship Akademik Lomonosov was named after Academician Mikhail Lomonosov.\n- Plans were announced to begin shutting down Bilibino Nuclear Power Plant in 2019.\n- Bilibino Nuclear Power Plant was to be replaced by the floating nuclear power station Akademik Lomonosov.",
